Description: Implements finite mixture regression models for Gaussian, Poisson, and
    binomial responses, with procedures for selecting covariates and
    determining whether covariate effects are heterogeneous or homogeneous across
    mixture components. Estimation is performed using EM algorithms,
    with weighted least squares and structured QR decompositions for efficient matrix inversions
    in the M-step. The weighted significance test (WEST) used for the stepwise
    procedures is described in Gan, Chen and Feng (2024)
    <doi:10.1080/02664763.2024.2433567>.
